Carafe: dxvk.shaderCompilationMethod (or DXVK_SHADER_COMPILATION_METHOD) carries DXVK-Sarek's choice of how
pipelines are built over to DXVK 3. With "async", a draw whose pipeline cannot be linked at once from ready shader
libraries is skipped, and the pipeline is compiled in full on a high-priority worker; the draw comes back once it
is ready, so the frame never waits for a compiler. "dyasync" builds the first pipeline of each shader set while
drawing, as before, and defers the later ones. Sarek's dyasync draws with a neighbouring variant meanwhile; DXVK 3
links such a stand-in from the shader libraries itself, and a variant built for other state would break Vulkan's
rules for dynamic state, so a deferred draw is skipped instead. "none", the default, keeps DXVK's behaviour.
Zlib, as the files it changes.

diff -ruN a/src/dxvk/dxvk_graphics.cpp b/src/dxvk/dxvk_graphics.cpp
